#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119488 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "9b2026e3-781b-5e73-8dc2-0e8f2789fe67" :question/math-academy-id "e-3065" :question/problem "Consider the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle 2t-1,\\: 8t+2,\\: -2t \\right\\rangle, \\, t \\geq 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf{r}(0)$ to $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is given by $s=6\\sqrt{2}t$. Find $\\mathbf R(s)$, the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s$." :question/worked-solution "First, since\n\n$$\ns=6\\sqrt{2}t\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6\\sqrt{2}t &= s \\\\\nt &= \\frac{s}{6\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with\n\n$$\ns \\geq 0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR(s) &= r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) \\\\\n&= ⟨2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) - 1, 8(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) + 2,-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6} - 1, \\frac{4\\sqrt{2}s}{6} + 2,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{2}s - 6, 4\\sqrt{2}s + 12,-\\sqrt{2}s⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119489 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "74f33486-6391-5ec0-8a5b-bb51c9af2d55" :question/math-academy-id "e-3066" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=2(t\\cos{t}-\\sin{t})\\,\\mathbf i+2(t\\sin{t}+\\cos{t})\\,\\mathbf j, \\, t \\geq 0$ by its arc length $s$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and its magnitude $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{′}(t) &= 2\\frac{d}{dt}(t\\cos t - \\sin t)i + 2\\frac{d}{dt}(t\\sin t + \\cos t)j \\\\\n&= 2(\\cos t - t\\sin t - \\cos t)i + 2(\\sin t + t\\cos t - \\sin t)j \\\\\n&=-2t\\sin ti + 2t\\cos tj \\\\\n‖r^{′}(t)‖ &= \\mid 2t \\mid \\sqrt{(-\\sin t)^{2} + \\cos^{2} t} \\\\\n&= 2t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the last step, we removed the absolute value bars since $t>0$.\n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns &= ∫_{0}^{t}‖r^{′}(u)‖du \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{t}2udu \\\\\n&= u^{2} \\mid _{0}^{t} \\\\\n&= t^{2} - 0 \\\\\n&= t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $s=t^2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt^{2} &= s \\\\\nt &= ± \\sqrt{s} \\\\\nt &= \\sqrt{s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ntaking the positive root because $t>0$.\n\nFinally, the vector function that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR(s) &= r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\\n&= 2(\\sqrt{s}\\cos \\sqrt{s} - \\sin \\sqrt{s})i + 2(\\sqrt{s}\\sin \\sqrt{s} + \\cos \\sqrt{s})j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "48350682-3ad0-5311-bb47-782ec454390c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3067" :question/problem "Given the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{t}\\,\\mathbf i - \\sin{t}\\,\\mathbf j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,\\mathbf k, \\, t \\geq 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by $s=2t$, find the corresponding unit tangent $\\mathbf{T}(s)$, parametrized by $s$." :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=2t$, we have that\n\n$$\nt=\\dfrac{s}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $\\mathbf R(s)$ that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR(s) &= r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{s}{2})i - \\sin (\\frac{s}{2})j + \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{s}{2}k \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{s}{2})i - \\sin (\\frac{s}{2})j + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}s}\\mathbf R(s)\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(s) &= \\frac{d}{ds}R(s) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{ds}(\\cos (\\frac{s}{2}))i + \\frac{d}{ds}(-\\sin (\\frac{s}{2}))j + \\frac{d}{ds}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2})k \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{s}{2})i - \\frac{1}{2}\\cos (\\frac{s}{2})j + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}k \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(-\\sin (\\frac{s}{2})i - \\cos (\\frac{s}{2})j + \\sqrt{3}k)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b07103c9-fa65-54ec-9e1c-b4200f1f6ff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨2s, 7 + 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117773} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8daa73-6df9-5f12-a4fa-b5c4216fbdae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = \\frac{1}{7}⟨2s, 7 - 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117774} {:answer/id #uuid "db2cd360-5297-5102-a6b8-7799dfdce2f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = \\frac{1}{7}⟨2s, 7 + 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117775} {:answer/id #uuid "eb67ca1a-2ae5-5677-8e21-aec2aff9639a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨2s, 7 - 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117776} {:answer/id #uuid "3413cc0d-dc91-5426-9eb4-af27ce15a12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = \\frac{1}{7}⟨2s, 1 - 3s, 5 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce8daa73-6df9-5f12-a4fa-b5c4216fbdae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = \\frac{1}{7}⟨2s, 7 - 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117774} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef45a99a-4388-5437-8221-7c3fd92de1c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117772}] :question/id #uuid "cd2d22fe-d6c9-55e5-8f32-f782e37e2d9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33860" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t) = ⟨2t, 1 - 3t, 5 + 6t⟩$, $t \\ge 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s = 7t$. Find $R(s)$, the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4a156a3-783f-5d10-b422-c497a68d4c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) = \\frac{4}{5}\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i - \\frac{4}{5}\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117779} {:answer/id #uuid "d4857719-2940-5346-a8a4-e8945f085695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) = 80\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i - 80\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117780} {:answer/id #uuid "2d81c4a8-2d2d-50a1-a49b-7d5f2500929d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) =-\\frac{4}{5}\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i + \\frac{4}{5}\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117781} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab216cc-6fb0-5693-8416-65e96019935f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) =-80\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i + 80\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117782} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecde1f9-3dd3-5990-81db-ddd2c538e8dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) =-\\frac{4}{5}\\sin (10s)i + \\frac{4}{5}\\cos (10s)j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d81c4a8-2d2d-50a1-a4